    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "Which Azure Cosmos DB API does this skill cover?",
        "answer": "It covers the Azure Cosmos DB NoSQL API through the azure_data_cosmos Rust package."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which authentication method is recommended?",
        "answer": "The examples prefer Entra ID through DeveloperToolsCredential. Key authentication is available through an optional package feature."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does the skill include item CRUD operations?",
        "answer": "Yes. It shows create, read, replace, patch, and delete patterns for typed Rust documents."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it provide query examples?",
        "answer": "No. The source describes item operations but does not demonstrate queries, pagination, or continuation tokens."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why is a partition key required?",
        "answer": "Cosmos DB uses the partition key to route point reads and writes to the correct logical partition."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can the examples run without changes?",
        "answer": "No. You must provide an endpoint, identity, permissions, database, container, and document model for your environment."
